  "1_pins": "PASS (parent): every input port lands in its face / entry region (pin register in fdn / fup, or the landing ring at the pin for fn / frs entries); every output leaves from a face-region flop. rst_n -> lp reset runs (depth 10, last stage = regional_reset_copies <= 32 loads) -> each leaf's own 2-stage landing (s6 face / tap leaves: second stage = kept copies <= 32 loads; closed children: their own landing). OPEN: the 182 slice<->slice face landings (plan claude/qw-slice4-face-1019) are NOT in this parent yet.",
  "2_reach": "OPEN / measured by the gate: cross-region nets are landings (E=4: <= ~2.6 mm per landing window); the face<->face pass crossings (fdn <-> fup now 1944 um: chu_q, hr, cmd, chd, treq, l9) EXCEED that window after the enlargement -> next GEN: a relay pad stage on those landings (lp pads, priced) or the D8/E4 fallback; the N<->S corridor (rs_n, cw_s 2.2 mm) unchanged; SU gb/pd1 group relay su8 -> lrly <= ~1.2 mm (r_su region: single-cycle reach measured by the gate textbook, lrly RD relays); 1-bit reset runs hop <= 405 um (lp reach)",
  "3_fanout": "PENDING parent mapped census: w6 failed8281roots; new n32 split/chunk writer max26 local mapped, hard xleaf pin/lib identical strictlintPASS; sc2/red2/xh3 replace old soft leaves. Prior structural plan: landing_chunk_bits 24 (kept per-chunk selectors: the e5 census rc[1]/exp_ 6,275 / sel 3,135 per landing is gone), > 32-chunk landings on ot_pl_land_split (rsi per 32 chunks), regional_reset_copies (kept copies <= 32), s6 face/tap leaves valid-only reset with kept copies; the pre-gate census of THIS kit is the proof (README census table)",
  "4_depth": "PASS (parent): wires only between children; landing read = registered slot select",
  "5_storage": "PASS: every SRAM / ROM inside a hard child (VM8 split leaves 18 SRAM, btab_s4 4 SRAM, tload ns4 4 ROM); landing rings D=8 are fixed-latency landings (238088 flops)",
  "6_floorplan": "PASS (plan): ENLARGED IN Y 2462.376 x 4319.976 (QW2-NEXTGEN reticle slot: +1684.8 VM8 band = VM8 group + su8 + 8 lane relays; same area as the 4060.8 x 2592 COORD slot); hard children on the 43.2 lattice (8 stnrgc, 8 heads, 24 SFU, 8 lrly, ctl5, su8, stream, tload, btab_s4, 7 VM8 leaves), no parent macros; relay channels <= 405 um apart; parent pins <= 4.54/um per port group",
  "7_clock": "multiple_cts_roots: 19 regional roots (ck_r_*), entry on the nearest face beside the region's register mass; fences hold every soft leaf + its landing read halves; judged per region at child flops (TT / FF spread <= 80); io_hold_margin 0.03",
  "8_schedule": "static; compiler record results/arch/codex_slice2_native_1021/s8/qfd_dv_s8b_lp_record.json: every cross-region reader pin +5 edges (lp lag_pins, slice loops); leaf HARD registers as s5 (ctl bundles / VM writes / own word / ag, stm tw, fdn pc_bad, tap cid); closed children: SU8 command visible +4 / reset +1 (Codex 5949f90af record), VM8 P3 VM reads/writes +1 vs P2 (+0 vs vm8fh on VM reads, +2 BTAB/PROG, +4 CROM), reset +2; stream c3r +1 a pass/tap, -1 own write; tload ns4 CAPTURE_STAGE 1; s6 face/tap leaves +0 (reset release edge unchanged); landing chunks / reset copies / split landings +0 edges",
  "stand_ins": "SOFT in this kit: sc, red, xhead x4 (successor kits: QW-S5-SCRED / QW-S5-XHEAD), x leaves x32 (w130 view legacy M6 abstract, pocket LEF owed), fdn / fup / tap (s6 census-safe leaves, no kit yet), u_suvm.u_vm8q glue SOFT (its 7 split leaves hard at the qfd_dv_slice2_vm8q P3 child layout; vm8q / vm8qb gates running, no view yet)"
